<title>FRANCE: SGS-Thomson sees 98 margin 40-42 pct.</title>
<headline>SGS-Thomson sees 98 margin 40-42 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Semiconductor group SGS-Thomson chairman Pasquale Pistorio said on Thursday that the company's gross margin in 1998 would be in a range of 40 to 42 percent.</p>
<p>He said he expected the rise in margins because &quot;we are at the start of a new upward cycle&quot;.</p>
<p>Asked whether a margin of 40 percent was possible in the fourth quarter of 1997, he said: &quot;It is desirable but difficult. We are working toward that.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
